{"base_rate":0.4195323246217332,"brier":0.17942187070151305,"bss":0.26323003729313976,"bss_hi":0.36335468737462423,"bss_lo":0.15662404579771352,"country":"LU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.13962861072902338,"ess":302.75560654363125,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Luxembourg</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Luxembourg rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 727 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-01. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nLUXEMBOURG AIRPORT, 5.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.26, ranked 78 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(43&ndash;96) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>290</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>33%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>222</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Luxembourg</b> <span class=\"muted\">LU</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.26</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>43&ndash;96\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>727 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Luxembourg &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Luxembourg\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.80758620689655,374.4689655172414 124.29013698630136,282.2739726027397 247.41424657534247,147.64383561643834 350.3834782608696,49.6521739130435 409.68783783783783,18.0 409.68783783783783,24.55855855855856 350.3834782608696,112.95652173913044 247.41424657534247,232.4109589041096 124.29013698630136,342.1095890410959 60.80758620689655,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"229.29023383768913\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"229.29023383768913\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.80758620689655,348.11034482758623 124.29013698630136,262.32876712328766 247.41424657534247,177.56164383561642 350.3834782608696,149.8840579710145 409.68783783783783,104.90090090090092\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 290 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.80758620689655\" cy=\"348.11034482758623\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 33% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"124.29013698630136\" cy=\"262.32876712328766\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"247.41424657534247\" cy=\"177.56164383561642\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 64% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"350.3834782608696\" cy=\"149.8840579710145\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 222 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.68783783783783\" cy=\"104.90090090090092\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Luxembourg the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.04).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.040</td><td class='num'>17.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>188</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.177</td><td class='num'>10.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.358</td><td class='num'>12.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.379</td><td class='num'>12.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":49.6116,"lon":6.1319,"n":727,"n_cities":109,"name":"Luxembourg","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00793103448275862,"n":290,"obs":0.09310344827586207,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.18726027397260273,"n":73,"obs":0.3287671232876712,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7060000000000007,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.5350684931506849,"n":73,"obs":0.5616438356164384,"sig":false},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.7060000000000007,"mean":0.8259420289855074,"n":69,"obs":0.6376811594202898,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9934684684684685,"n":222,"obs":0.7612612612612613,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.4,"rank":78,"rank_hi":96.02499999999998,"rank_lo":43.0,"reliability":0.024804498989933407,"resolution":0.08553695526911094,"slug":"luxembourg","station":"LUXEMBOURG AIRPORT","timezone":"Europe/Luxembourg"}